@* What every sample page shows above its document: who has it open, where its connection stands, and a switch that
   takes it offline on purpose. Place it inside a BcrdtCollaborationScope, which cascades the open document. *@

<div class="status">
    <BcrdtPresenceView Presence="Document.Presence" />

    @* Synced, reconnecting, offline - with when it last synced - and "read-only" when the server granted read access
       only. The MAUI host registers no transport by default, and then it says "local only": the document is this
       device's alone, and still persisted. The button is a deliberate disconnect: the document stays editable, and the
       handshake on reconnect sends each side whatever the other wrote meanwhile. *@
    <BcrdtSyncStatus Class="muted" ShowToggle="true" />
</div>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter] public BcrdtCollaborativeDocument Document { get; set; } = default!;
}
